      origins: 'Stortok is known from three documented sources: Lindskog (1847), Öberg (1858), and Schenkmanis (1980s, also in Norwegian as Kjempetosk). It is a Swedish beating game related to Durak, with two trump suits (high and low by colour). The 1847 and 1858 accounts differ from the late 20th-century version in deal size, trick structure, and lead rules.',
