          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "To get rid of all one's cards. The last player left with cards is the loser and is called the Great Fool (Stortok).",
          gameplay: 'Forehand (left of dealer) leads any card to start the play pile. Each player in turn must beat the top card (same suit higher, or any trump on non-trump, or high trump on low trump) or pick up the whole play pile. When everyone has beaten, the trick is complete and the last player to play leads the next. When a player picks up, the player to their right (who played the highest card in the incomplete trick) leads. So long as the stock has cards, after each card played the player draws one from the stock. When the stock is exhausted, play continues until one player remains with cards; that player is the Stortok (loser).',
          keyRules: [
            'Same suit: higher rank beats. Non-trump beaten by any low or high trump. Low trump beaten by any high trump.',
            'Pick up the whole play pile if unable or unwilling to beat the top card.',
            'Draw one from stock after each play while stock has cards.',
            'Last player with cards is the Stortok (Great Fool).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Save high trumps for defense. Don't waste them on low non-trumps unless necessary. Try to attack with pairs if allowed (to force defender to use two good cards).",
          intermediate: 'Hand Management: Keep a variety of suits to avoid being forced to trump unnecessarily.',
          advanced: 'Card Counting: Remember which trumps have been played. If the Ace of Trumps is gone, the King is boss.',
          tips: [
            'The goal is not to win tricks, but to shed.',
            'Attacking drains your hand, which is good.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
